From a248724637888f276c605a5fbebadc5acb9e3025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:19:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] patches/openwrt: nvmem: don't defer forever on a missing
 layout cell

A consumer of an NVMEM cell never probes if the layout of the NVMEM
device is bound but did not add the cell. Return -ENOENT instead of
-EPROBE_DEFER once the layout device is bound, so that the consumer can
fall back to another address. The AMIT P-section layout in the next
patch relies on it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
